In `xarray/core/missing.py`, `get_clean_interp_index` ends by attempting `index.values.astype(np.float64)` inside a `try`. The corresponding `except (TypeError, ValueError) as err` shows the cast failure can be one of those two kinds, and the handler immediately raises a new `TypeError` from that caught error. The QA test constructs two non-float-castable indexes and expects `TypeError` from each call, so the exception kinds seen in that failing cast-plus-handler sequence are the original `ValueError` from the cast and then the handler’s `TypeError`, in that order.

## Answer
{"caught_exception_kinds":["ValueError","TypeError"]}
